 r←IsUpdateCandidate report
⍝ Takes one of the matrices Tatin's `CheckForLaterVersion` returns and marks with a 1 exactly
⍝ those rows that offer a later version of an installed package.\\
⍝ Column [;4] does not answer that question, although it looks as if it should: Tatin also sets
⍝ it when the very same version turned up on a different Registry, which is worth knowing but is
⍝ not an update. Column [;2] is the one to go by, but it may carry a marker like
⍝ "<<< Not available any more >>>" instead of a package ID, and it repeats [;1] when nothing
⍝ later was found. So a row offers an update when [;2] names a package ID other than [;1].\\
⍝ See `ReportPackageProblems` for what happens to the rows this leaves out.
 r←('<'≠⊃¨report[;2])∧report[;1]≢¨report[;2]
⍝Done
